{
  "name": "Vet TikTok and Instagram creators from Google Sheets with API.SH",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Vet TikTok and Instagram creators from a Google Sheet\n\n### How it works\nPaste creator handles into a Google Sheet and run the workflow. It cleans each handle (an @name, a plain username or a profile URL all work), looks up the public TikTok and Instagram profiles with the **API.SH** node, and writes back followers, verification, TikTok likes per video, an engagement signal (likes per video ÷ followers), total reach and a size tier (nano to mega). Empty cells are skipped, and private accounts or failed lookups are noted in the `notes` column instead of stopping the run, so you can shortlist creators before reaching out.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the verified **API.SH** node (nodes panel → search \"API.SH\") and add your API key from [api.sh](https://api.sh). Each profile is 1 credit; every account gets 1,000 free credits a month.\n2. Create a Google Sheet with a tab named **Creators** and headers: `tiktok`, `instagram`, `tiktok_followers`, `tiktok_videos`, `tiktok_likes_per_video`, `tiktok_engagement_percent`, `tiktok_verified`, `instagram_followers`, `instagram_verified`, `instagram_bio`, `total_reach`, `tier`, `notes`, `checked_at`.\n3. Paste the sheet URL into both Google Sheets nodes and connect your Google account.\n\n### Customization\nSwap the manual trigger for a weekly schedule to track growth, or add the API.SH `/tiktok/v1/channel` endpoint to score recent videos instead of lifetime likes.",
        "height": 780,
        "width": 480
      },
      "id": "44587810-50ee-4180-997f-e8fca227747e",
